<newsitem itemid="28010" id="root" date="1996-09-02" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Bunzl posts 12 percent rise in H1 profits.</title>
<headline>Bunzl posts 12 percent rise in H1 profits.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		8.1		    vs 7.4</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 2.2		    vs 2.0</p>
<p> Pretax profit	    55.8		   vs 50.0</p>
<p> Turnover		   887.5		  vs 879.5</p>
<p> Operating profit	 54.7		   vs 51.4</p>
<p> Interest paid	    0.4		    vs 1.4</p>
<p> Tax paid		   19.5		   vs 17.5</p>
<p> Net taxed		  36.3		   vs 32.5</p>
<p>NOTE - Paper and plastics group Bunzl Plc said it had shown  </p>
<p>a strong operating performance in the first half, despite deflationary pressures in most parts of its business. This reflected continued improvement in margins, tight control of costs and good cash management, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
